WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:06.120
After Toy Story 3's almost perfect ending,
Pixar has brought the toys back for a sequel

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.070
that's positively bursting with easter eggs
and amazing hidden details.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:15.049
The movie has call-backs and deep-cut references
to every single Pixar film so far.

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:19.000
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'll be helping you navigate the

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.650
maze of Pixar easter eggs, in-jokes, and crucial
details you might have missed in Toy Story

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.301
4.
There are some mild spoilers ahead, though

00:00:26.301 --> 00:00:31.450
I avoid discussing any major plot points.
And a new Toy Story giveaway just started

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:36.100
on this video, so subscribe, hit the bell
and let me know which easter eggs you spotted

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.559
for a chance to win.

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:42.429
Let's kick things off with a nostalgic easter
egg to Up when Woody reunites with Bo Peep

00:00:42.429 --> 00:00:45.739
at the carnival.
When Bo's sheep bring her a bottle top, look

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:49.829
closely as it's the grape soda pin that Ellie
gave Carl when they were kids.

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:54.420
"You and me, we're in a club now."
Carl also gave the pin to Russell at the end

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.559
of that movie and it's a nice touch by Pixar
to include it in Toy Story 4 when Woody and

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:03.659
Bo reunite as it links back to the love that
Carl and Ellie shared in Up.

00:01:03.659 --> 00:01:10.590
And powering Bo's skunk car are some BnL batteries.
BnL, aka Buy n Large, is the corporation in

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.509
WALL•E that basically enabled the pollution
of the planet and sent humans away from Earth

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:16.600
while it attempted to clear it up.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.460
Pixar always includes an easter egg to its
next movie and for Onward you'll need to look

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.890
carefully among the various attractions at
the Carnival.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.040
There's a stand called Dragon Zone which also
has a little dragon on its banner.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.390
"Blazey! Down!
Sorry, I didn't get a chance to walk her.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.020
Oh! Bad dragon!
Back to your lair!"

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.530
Pixar's famous Pizza Planet Truck has also
been hidden at the carnival in a very curious

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.399
way.
Keep your eyes focused on the carnival worker

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:44.859
who runs the game booth where Ducky and Bunny
are prizes.

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:49.539
You can see the truck for just a split second
as a tattoo on the back of his leg in this

00:01:49.539 --> 00:01:53.570
scene where he knocks Buzz over.
By the way, the official Art of Toy Story

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.630
4 book shows that the design of the Pizza
Planet truck tattoo is styled in a similar

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.950
fashion to the flaming targets at the carnie's
game booth.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.390
The Pizza Planet truck appeared in the very
first Toy Story movie and is a regular Pixar

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.710
easter egg.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.130
The stand also has lots more easter eggs hidden
among the toys.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:15.090
There's a couple of tiny red and white rockets
attached to a toy planet with a similar look

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:19.400
to the iconic red and white Pizza Planet rocket
from the Pizza Planet restaurant in the first

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.790
Toy Story movie.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.160
Another similar rocket design also appears
on some of the caps at the game booth.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:30.050
There are also several toy guitars with designs
and patterns similar to the guitar that Miguel

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:34.019
took from Ernesto de la Cruz's mausoleum in
Coco.

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:39.720
Other prizes include some rockets labelled
X-99, a nod to Toy Story 2 which was released

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.720
in 1999.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:46.120
And the red star on a yellow circle with blue
stripes to the side is a little Luxo ball

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.409
easter egg.
The full Luxo ball appears in the antique

00:02:49.409 --> 00:02:52.780
shop and I'll be getting to that easter egg
very shortly.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:57.320
The green frog here also looks very similar
to one of the garbage truck toys that Lotso

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.080
joined when he was picked up by the driver
at the end of Toy Story 3.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:06.090
"Hey, buddy, you might wanna keep your mouth
shut."

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:10.780
Toy Story 4 has an interesting connection
with the Pixar short Toy Story of Terror via

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.849
the Ship It truck which you can spot parked
outside the antiques store.

00:03:14.849 --> 00:03:19.439
Ship It was the delivery company that was
picking up packages from the Sleep Well Motel

00:03:19.439 --> 00:03:23.470
in Toy Story of Terror.
And it's also the same truck that Combat Carl

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:28.540
and some other toys hopped on in the short's
closing credits to escape from Ron, the motel

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.659
manager who was stealing toys to sell them
on the internet.

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.920
"Next stop, Billy's house"

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:39.030
This one's tricky to spot, but the same wooden
cart plus balloons that Carl from Up had when

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.830
he was a balloon salesman appears at the carnival.

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:47.459
Also at the carnival is a truck with a clown
painted on the side, a reference to the 1987

00:03:47.459 --> 00:03:50.090
Pixar short film Red Stream.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:53.930
When Woody and the gang open up a hatch on
the roof of the antique store, the famous

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.819
Pixar Luxo ball appears on the floor below
them for just a split second.

00:03:57.819 --> 00:04:03.450
The Luxo ball is a regular Pixar easter egg
and an homage to the animation studio's first

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.670
short film, Luxo Jr.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:10.670
Inside the store is a veritable cornucopia
of vintage objects and Pixar easter eggs.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:15.340
There's a box of Casey Jr Cookies which were
used in A Bug's Life as wagons to transport

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:18.910
P.T. Flea's circus.
And, of course, they're also a Disney reference

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.130
to the steam train which transported the circus
in Dumbo.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:27.250
Next to the Casey Jr Cookies is the diving
mask that belonged to the dentist in Finding

00:04:27.250 --> 00:04:28.250
Nemo.

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:32.160
And Carl's cane from Up is also there hidden
away on an upper shelf.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:38.900
"Where's my cane I just had it here?"

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:43.370
On the wall in the store is a painting that
references the scene in Up where Russell passes

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:47.620
a group of dogs playing poker.
In this painting, Charles Muntz and Dug the

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:53.170
dog have also been added to the gambling table.
The original scene in Up was itself a reference

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:57.610
to a famous series of paintings of dogs playing
cards which were commissioned to advertise

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.130
cigars.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:03.600
Also hanging on the wall is an unlit sign
for Dinoco, the oil company and gas station

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.670
that's appeared in Pixar films including the
Toy Story and Cars movies.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:12.240
Bonnie and her family also stop for gas at
a Dinoco during their road trip.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.610
It's tricky to see but there's a miniature
black Ford Model T toy on one of the shelves,

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:19.389
a nod to Lizzie from the Cars movies.

00:05:19.389 --> 00:05:24.160
You can spot another Cars reference on a licence
plate during the Forky rescue attempt.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.699
There's Carb County, short for Carburetor
County, which is where Radiator Springs is

00:05:28.699 --> 00:05:29.880
located.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.520
And above the licence number is Torqueville,
another location in the Cars universe.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:40.410
As the toys flee from Gabby Gabby's ventriloquist
dummies, they fly past an old-looking square

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:45.289
box with the word "Pixar" on it.
This is a vintage 80s Pixar Image Computer,

00:05:45.289 --> 00:05:50.319
a graphics machine developed by the company
back in the days when it belonged to Lucasfilm.

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:54.910
You can also see it used as the logo in some
of Pixar's older short films.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.290
When Bo slides through Gabby Gabby's cabinet,
there's a commemorative plate with a symbol

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:04.410
that fans of Pixar's Brave will recognise
as the sword symbol represents King Fergus

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:05.610
and Merida's clan.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:11.270
When Bo takes Woody to meet Duke Caboom inside
the store, they go to a secret toy hang-out

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.400
inside a pinball machine.
The Art of Toy Story 4 book shows that the

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.539
arcade machine is called "Tiki Party", a reference
to the Tiki heads inside the fish tank from

00:06:20.539 --> 00:06:21.539
Finding Nemo.

00:06:21.539 --> 00:06:25.470
And there are some great easter eggs inside
the pinball machine.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:31.260
The first one is Tinny, a one-man band player
who originally appeared in the 1998 Pixar

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:34.389
short film Tin Toy.
Tinny was actually going to be one of the

00:06:34.389 --> 00:06:38.800
main protagonists of the original Toy Story
movie, until it was decided the toy was too

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.060
old-fashioned and he was replaced by Buzz
Lightyear.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:47.250
Also inside the toy hang-out are a couple
of vintage Star Wars toys for Obi-Wan Kenobi

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.310
and Ponda Baba.
The wonderful thing about this particular

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:55.530
easter egg is that if you look very carefully,
Obi-Wan Kenobi is repeatedly striking Ponda

00:06:55.530 --> 00:07:00.340
Baba on the arm with his lightsabre in an
awesome homage to the original Star Wars Cantina

00:07:00.340 --> 00:07:04.370
scene where Obi-Wan sliced off the Walrus
Man's arm.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:09.229
And there may be another Star Wars arm loss
reference when Woody accidentally pulls Bo's

00:07:09.229 --> 00:07:10.449
arm off.

00:07:10.449 --> 00:07:15.840
Franklin the toy bald eagle from the Toy Story
short "Small Fry" is also inside the pinball

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.650
machine.
Franklin was part of the discarded fun meal

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:22.980
toys support group in that short, so it makes
sense he's with the group of "lost toys" in

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.930
Toy Story 4.
"Why don't the kids like me?

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.490
I'm like history but on wheels!"

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:33.780
Bo and Woody finally get to meet Duke Caboom,
the Canadian stuntman toy who previously appeared

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:37.250
in Jack-Jack's crib as an easter egg in Incredibles
2.

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:41.780
When Duke Caboom does the jump from the Ferris
wheel, he passes across the moon in a little

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:46.370
homage not just to E.T., but also to when
Mater did a similar jump through the air in

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:47.830
the first Cars movie.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:52.190
Duke Caboom is voiced by Keanu Reeves, and
it's an especially fitting role for the actor

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:56.659
as not only has Reeves starred in many action
movies including John Wick, The Matrix, and

00:07:56.659 --> 00:08:02.510
Speed, but he's also a keen motorcyclist and
even co-owns a company that makes custom motorcycles.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:05.759
"Duke Caboom!
Canada's greatest stuntman!

00:08:05.759 --> 00:08:09.560
Huh. Oh yeah!
Ha. Huh. Yes."

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:14.300
And as Caboom, Reeves also gets to deliver
his famous "Whoa" line from Bill and Ted's

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.990
Excellent Adventure in the movie's mid-credits.
"Whoa!"

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:22.889
For more on Toy Story 4's post-credits, check
out the second part of my easter egg guide

00:08:22.889 --> 00:08:24.490
which I'll link to at the end of this video.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:29.110
As for the voice of the TV announcer on the
Duke Caboom commercial, that's Flea from the

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:33.450
Red Hot Chilli Peppers.
"He's the most spectacular daredevil Canada

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.690
has ever seen!"

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:40.400
The A113 easter egg is a regular Pixar one
that proved a little tougher than usual to

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:45.470
spot in Toy Story 4 compared to previous movies
where it's often simply appeared on licence

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.220
plates or written on walls.
This time, you'll see it in Second Chance

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:55.620
Antiques but as a vintage 70s-style sign.
The appearance of A113 in Pixar's films is

00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:00.730
a tribute to the classroom at California Institute
of the Arts where many of Pixar's animators

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.090
studied.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:06.340
Other vintage sign easter eggs to look out
for in the store include this one for "Ye

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:09.650
Olde Poultry Palace".
Poultry Palace is the chicken restaurant that

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:13.090
featured in the Toy Story Toon short "Small
Fry"

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:17.250
And in Toy Story 4, Bonnie and her family
also visit the fast food chain during their

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.250
road trip.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:22.480
There's an old record player in the antique
store with an Ernesto de la Cruz greatest

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.220
hits record.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:28.070
Keep your eyes peeled for a vintage ad for
TripleDent, which is the brand of chewing

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:30.920
gum with that very memorable jingle in Inside
Out!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.140
"The song from the gum commercial!"
"You know sometimes we send that one up to

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.270
headquarters for no reason."

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:40.390
There's a classic Eggman Moving Company sign
in the antique shop, an easter to the Eggman

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:43.640
Movers who appeared in the first Toy Story
film.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:47.930
And as Vincent the ventriloquist doll wheels
Gabby Gabby, Woody, and Forky away, another

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:52.140
old record starts playing.
The song is "Midnight, The Stars And You",

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:55.760
which played at the end of The Shining.
There've been numerous tributes to director

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:59.980
Stanley Kubrick's classic movie in Pixar's
films over the years including the carpet

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:04.510
in Sid's house in the first Toy Story movie
and various references to the horror film's

00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:06.910
creepy Room 237.
"Who's Velocistar237?"

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:13.950
"That's just a dinosaur toy down the street.
That's nothing. Let me just take care of that."

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:18.320
And there's another Kubrick homage when Buzz
presses one of his buttons and his inner voice

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:24.060
says 'Open the pod bay doors', which is a
famous line from 2001: A Space Odyssey.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:28.320
Ducky and Bunny's fantasy sequences about
how to get the key from the antique store

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:32.310
owner are particularly hilarious.
"What about the old plush rush?"

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:37.060
"There you go."
"Oh, where did you two come from?"

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:41.170
"Give us the keys!"
"Well we're not doing that."

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:45.310
And in another scenario, when the old lady
opens her fridge at home, we get a glimpse

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:49.190
at another regular Pixar easter egg: the Chinese
take-out box.

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:52.951
The box has a very specific design and has
appeared in the back of the Pizza Planet Truck

00:10:52.951 --> 00:10:58.270
in Toy Story 2, in Inside Out, Monsters Inc,
Ratatouille, and also Incredibles 2.

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:06.290
Its first appearance was in A Bug's Life where
it was called "the Chinese Cabinet of Metamorphosis".

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:10.440
There's a ton more Pixar objects in Second
Chance Antiques and I'll run through a quick

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:14.560
list of some to look out for.
Elastigirl's Elasticycle from Incredibles

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.560
2 can be seen as a toy in the store.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:20.480
There's also one of the Monsters Inc scream
canisters for sale.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.670
And there's a bear carving from Brave.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:26.480
The house from Up which Carl so memorably
took on a balloon journey has been shrunk

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:29.410
down into a doll house and is now for sale.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:32.250
Bing Bong's Rocket from Inside Out also appears.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:37.120
Plus, there are board games for two Pixar
shorts, "Knick Knack" and "Lifted".

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:40.240
The antique store itself is also a double
easter egg.

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:45.930
Firstly, the address number is 1200, a reference
to 1200 Park Avenue in Emeryville, the address

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.290
of Pixar Animation Studios.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:53.230
And Second Chance Antiques was founded in
1986, the same year Pixar was spun out as

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.370
a separate corporation from Lucasfilm.

00:11:55.370 --> 00:12:00.060
We've also got some very cool easter eggs
to talk about from the movie's opening flashback

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:04.420
scene, plus an intriguing change that Pixar
made to Toy Story 4 that could completely

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:07.930
debunk the Pixar Theory.
Those will be all in the second part of this

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.760
video.
I'll add the link here and in the video description

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:12.630
for you to watch as soon as it's ready.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.100
So, which easter eggs did you spot in Toy
Story 4?

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.240
And are there any I missed?
Share your thoughts in the comments below

